third ventricle

999
00:51:21,130 --> 00:51:24,270
and then by here
you can see sort of

1000
00:51:24,270 --> 00:51:27,310
that full division
now there are still

1001
00:51:27,310 --> 00:51:29,670
interventricular foramina
that will connect

1002
00:51:29,670 --> 00:51:31,790
the lateral to the
third ventricles

1003
00:51:31,790 --> 00:51:34,710
but they've gotten
smaller at this point

1004
00:51:34,710 --> 00:51:36,830
they're just a small
foramina and you

1005
00:51:36,830 --> 00:51:39,130
can only see through
a particular slice

1006
00:51:39,310 --> 00:51:42,860
and so here's sort
of our general setup

1007
00:51:42,860 --> 00:51:45,210
in the end and you
can see that there's

1008
00:51:45,210 --> 00:51:47,890
choroid plexus
growing into each of

1009
00:51:47,890 --> 00:51:50,290
the ventricles each
lateral ventricle and

1010
00:51:50,290 --> 00:51:52,130
the third ventricle
all have choroid

1011
00:51:52,130 --> 00:51:54,450
plexus and so does
the fourth ventricle

1012
00:51:56,230 --> 00:51:58,750
and that lateral
ventricle grows along with

1013
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:01,570
the cerebrum so it's
the white space here

1014
00:52:01,570 --> 00:52:04,410
inside the cerebrum
and as the cerebral

1015
00:52:04,410 --> 00:52:06,750
hemispheres grow that
lateral ventricle sort

1016
00:52:06,750 --> 00:52:08,730
of grows different horns
here. So we have that

1017
00:52:08,730 --> 00:52:10,550
temporal horn going
out into the temporal

1018
00:52:10,550 --> 00:52:14,030
lobe, and then lastly
