and cerebrospinal fluid

1042
00:53:25,530 --> 00:53:28,230
cannot do what I just
described, and flow

1043
00:53:28,230 --> 00:53:31,140
from the lateral to
the third ventricle

1044
00:53:31,510 --> 00:53:33,890
through the aqueduct,
into the fourth ventricle,

1045
00:53:33,890 --> 00:53:35,850
and then into the
subarachnoid space.

1046
00:53:36,750 --> 00:53:39,530
So if cerebrospinal
fluid can't drain

1047
00:53:39,530 --> 00:53:41,830
properly, it builds up
within those ventricles,

1048
00:53:41,830 --> 00:53:44,490
and those push
outward on the brain,

1049
00:53:44,490 --> 00:53:46,470
and the brain pushes
outward on the skull,

1050
00:53:46,470 --> 00:53:49,410
and everything gets
sort of enlarged

1051
00:53:49,410 --> 00:53:52,550
here. So signs of this
include large head

1052
00:53:52,550 --> 00:53:56,190
