remember that in infants,

1054
00:53:58,890 --> 00:54:01,510
the bones of the
calvarium are not all

1055
00:54:01,510 --> 00:54:03,510
sutured together, and
there are membranous

1056
00:54:03,510 --> 00:54:06,210
portions there called
fontanelles, and

1057
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:08,470
so those fontanelles
will bulge outward.

1058
00:54:09,630 --> 00:54:11,590
And in terms of symptoms,

1059
00:54:12,150 --> 00:54:13,310
right, general sort of

1060
00:54:13,310 --> 00:54:14,850
irritability, drowsiness,

1061
00:54:15,090 --> 00:54:18,390
vomiting seizures,
that kind of thing is

1062
00:54:18,390 --> 00:54:19,940
what you're going to
see with hydrocephalus.

1063
00:54:23,190 --> 00:54:26,010
So summing it all
up, remember that

1064
00:54:26,010 --> 00:54:27,390
the nervous system
develops from

1065
00:54:27,390 --> 00:54:30,350
ectoderm, and the
process of forming the

1066
00:54:30,350 --> 00:54:32,370
neural tube is
called neurulation.

1067
00:54:32,690 --> 00:54:35,910
Neural crest cells
then migrate from the

1068
00:54:35,910 --> 00:54:38,210
neural tube to form
parts of the peripheral

1069
00:54:38,210 --> 00:54:40,410
nervous system as well
as other structures.

1070
00:54:41,530 --> 00:54:43,910
Once that neural
tube is formed, it's

1071
00:54:43,910 --> 00:54:47,030
divided into basal
plates and alar plates.

1072
00:54:47,030 --> 00:54:48,750
The basal plates
are associated with

1073
00:54:48,750 --> 00:54:51,470
motor regions and the
alar plates with sensory

1074
00:54:51,470 --> 00:54:54,210
regions. The final
configuration

1075
00:54:54,210 --> 00:54:57,310
differs a bit between
the spinal cord and

1076
00:54:57,310 --> 00:55:00,490
the brain stem, so look
at those differences

1077
00:55:00,490 --> 00:55:02,170
to think about the
differentiation

1078
00:55:02,170 --> 00:55:04,730
between motor regions
and sensory regions.

1079
00:55:05,550 --> 00:55:09,750
And then finally, the
brain is formed by a

1080
00:55:09,750 --> 00:55:11,930
series of vesicles,
each of which is sort

1081
00:55:11,930 --> 00:55:15,650
of an inflated area
of the tube, and each

1082
00:55:15,650 --> 00:55:17,910
vesicle gives rise to
a portion of the brain

1083
00:55:17,910 --> 00:55:20,550
and a portion of the
ventricular system.

1084
